course: dictionary
lesson: 13230
title: Gauntleted
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Gauntleted describes a hand that is wearing a gauntlet. A gauntlet is a thick glove with a wide cuff that covers the wrist, or an armoured glove worn by a knight. «The knight pulled on his metal gauntlets before the battle.» The words metal and battle are clues that a gauntlet is strong and made for protection.
explain: Gauntleted is an adjective, so it tells you about a noun, usually a hand. «The falconer held out a gauntleted hand, and the hawk landed on it.» The hand is covered by a thick glove, so the hawk's claws cannot hurt it.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «The falconer held out a thick-gloved hand» in place of gauntleted hand. Does it still make sense? If it does, you have understood the word.
fact: A gauntlet is a thick glove with a wide cuff that covers the wrist.
fact: «Gauntleted» means wearing a gauntlet, or covered by one.
fact: Knights wore metal gauntlets to protect their hands in battle.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad dresses up in goggles, a cap and gauntlets when he drives his car.
fact: Falconers, bikers and fencers have also worn gauntlets to protect their hands.
exercise: «The knight raised his gauntleted hand to stop his men.» What does gauntleted mean? | *Wearing a thick glove with a wide cuff | Holding a sword in one hand | Empty and open | Covered in mud and sand
exercise: Find the word in «Toad gripped the wheel with his gauntleted hands» that describes his hands. | *gauntleted | gripped | wheel | Toad
exercise: Why might an author choose gauntleted instead of gloved? | It means the hands are wet from rain | It means the hands are very small | It is simply a longer word for hand | *It tells us the gloves are thick, with wide cuffs, like a knight's or a driver's
test: «The falconer held out a gauntleted hand for the hawk.» What is a gauntlet? | A saddle for a horse | A type of metal sword | A small bird that hunts | *A thick glove with a wide cuff that covers the wrist
test: In «The knight pulled on his metal gauntlets before the battle», which words are clues to the meaning? | Knight and before | The words are no help at all | Pulled and his | *Metal and battle
exam: «Dan's gauntleted hand gripped the handlebars as he rode his bike.» What does gauntleted mean in this sentence? | Holding a bell | Bare and cold in the wind | Dirty and wet from the road | *Wearing a thick glove with a wide cuff
